WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.700
Ancient India.

2
00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:05.200
Upali, a wealthy supporter
of the Jain teachers,

3
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.920
sets out to beat the Buddha in debate.

4
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.710
Instead, Upali is won over.

5
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.460
He asks to become the Buddha's follower.

6
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.630
Other teachers, Upali says, would have
paraded through the town with a convert

7
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:18.900
like him.

8
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.290
But the Buddha also tells him to
keep giving alms to his old teachers.

9
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.170
Why would he do that?

10
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.160
In this mission, you'll read
the Buddha's words to Upali,

11
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.600
then the stone edicts
of the emperor Ashoka.

12
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.650
Then you'll see how Buddhists today
meet other faiths and worldviews,

13
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.290
and where they draw firm lines.

14
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: find out why a new follower
is told to keep supporting his old teachers.
